                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_01\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit renames the package declaration in\nsrc/test/java/.../YuleApplicationTests.java from `com.github.piotr.rusin.yule`\n(dot-separated, mirroring the \"piotr rusin\" name literally) to\n`com.github.piotr_rusin.yule` (underscore, matching the rest of the\napplication's package structure). The fix commit message states this\nresolves a test initialization error caused by no application configuration\nbeing found \u2014 i.e. Spring's component/context scanning could not locate the\napplication context because the test class lived in a different package\ntree (`com.github.piotr.rusin.yule`) than the main application\n(`com.github.piotr_rusin.yule`).\n\nThe exact buggy line, `package com.github.piotr.rusin.yule;`, was first\nintroduced in candidate_01, which created the file\n`src/test/java/com/github/piotr/rusin/yule/YuleApplicationTests.java` from\nscratch with that package declaration (and also created the main\napplication class under the same dot-separated `com.github.piotr.rusin.yule`\npackage at that time, so the two were initially consistent with each other).\n\nCandidate_02 only added a license header block above the package line in\nthe test file and otherwise touched unrelated files (LICENSE, entity/Post.java\nlicense header, and confirmed that by this point the main source tree,\nPost.java and YuleApplication.java, had already been moved to the\n`com.github.piotr_rusin.yule` package \u2014 the `package` line in the test file\nitself was left completely untouched by candidate_02). This means the\nunderlying divergence (main app package renamed to use an underscore while\nthe test package retained the original dot-separated form) trace back to the\noriginal creation of the test file's package declaration in candidate_01;\nthat specific line was never modified again until the fix commit\n(candidate_03) corrected it.\n\nCandidate_03 is the fix commit itself (the rename that resolves the\nmismatch), not the bug-introducing commit.\n\nBecause the exact problematic line in the test file was authored in\ncandidate_01 and never subsequently modified until the fix, candidate_01 is\nthe commit that introduced the bug (the mismatched, dot-separated test\npackage that diverged from the underscore-based main application package,\ncausing Spring Boot test context loading to fail).\n"
